+### CLIP-NeRF
 A method that adds CLIP (a text-image pre-trained multimodal model) to provide greater freedom in shape operations and global deformation, using a disentangled conditional NeRF architecture [S2]. It applies a learned deformation network to shape modulation, embeds appearance codes into volume rendering to map color output, and allows control over both shape and appearance [S2].
 
-#### JacobiNeRF
-The model synthesizes a NeRF model based on second-order information (Jacobian matrix) to maximize mutual information between highly correlated entities under random scene perturbations. The rendering equation used is: $\hat{C}(r, z_s, z_c) = \sum_{i=1}^{N_c-1} c_i \alpha_i \exp\left(-\sum_{j=1}^{i-1} \sigma_j \delta_j\right)$, where $a_i = 1 - \exp(-\sigma_i \delta_i)$ is consistent with discrete volume rendering [S2].
+### JacobiNeRF
+The model synthesizes a NeRF model based on second-order information (Jacobian matrix) to maximize mutual information between highly correlated entities under random scene perturbations [S2]. The rendering equation used is: $\hat{C}(r, z_s, z_c) = \sum_{i=1}^{N_c-1} c_i \alpha_i \exp\left(-\sum_{j=1}^{i-1} \sigma_j \delta_j\right)$, where $a_i = 1 - \exp(-\sigma_i \delta_i)$ is consistent with discrete volume rendering [S2].
 
-#### DE-NeRF
-Decomposes lighting, geometry, and appearance to allow relighting of high-frequency environments and appearance editing [S3]. It trains a signed distance field (SDF) function using a set of 2D images to reconstruct a display grid as the input scene for the MLP. It decomposes the scene into geometric features and appearance features (diffuse reflection, roughness, specular tint). Input geometric features, appearance features, and distance h (from sampling point to grid) into four corresponding MLPs to predict diffuse albedo, roughness value, and specular tint. It integrates diffuse reflectance with the environment map to get diffuse color $c_d$. It trains a specular lighting MLP $F_s$ to get specular lighting $c_l$. It multiplies specular lighting $c_l$ with specular hue to get specular color $c_s$. It calculates final color $c$ as $c_s + c_d$. On NeRF Synthetic and Shiny Blender data sets, PSNR is 2 points higher than latest papers [S3].
+### RefSR-NeRF
+Reference-guided super-resolution neural radiation field framework combining NeRF and RefSR-CNN to achieve high-quality new perspective synthesis while balancing memory and speed [S3]. Stage 1 modifies NeRF sampling strategy to adopt patch ray sampling on the high-resolution input image to obtain a low-resolution image. RefSR-CNN yields feature maps from the detail-dominant information module and the degradation-dominant information module, which are fused to reconstruct a high-resolution image [S3]. On the NeRF-LLFF data set, PSNR is nearly one point higher than the best paper [S3].
 
-#### RefSR-NeRF
-Reference-guided super-resolution neural radiation field framework combining NeRF and RefSR-CNN to achieve high-quality new perspective synthesis while balancing memory and speed [S3]. Stage 1: Modify NeRF sampling strategy to adopt patch ray sampling on the high-resolution input image to obtain a low-resolution image. RefSR-CNN yields feature maps from the detail-dominant information module and the degradation-dominant information module. It fuses the two feature maps to reconstruct a high-resolution image. On the NeRF-LLFF data set, PSNR is nearly one point higher than the best paper [S3].
+### RelightingNeRF
+Proposed for handling unstructured photographs and free-viewpoint reconstruction, changing model architecture to output SDF values and latent features [S3]. Input sampling point position into the first MLP, which outputs SDF values and latent features. Normals, shadow cues, and specular cues are obtained from the SDF values. The second MLP takes sampling point positions, lighting positions, and viewing directions, along with latent features from the first MLP, to produce the final color [S3].
 
-#### RelightingNeRF
-Proposed for handling unstructured photographs and free-viewpoint reconstruction, changing model architecture to output SDF values and latent features [S3]. Input sampling point position into the first MLP, which outputs SDF values and latent features. It obtains normals, shadow cues, and specular cues from the SDF values. It provides sampling point positions, lighting positions, and viewing directions, along with latent features from the first MLP, to the second MLP. The second MLP produces the final color [S3].
+### DiffusioNeRF
+A method that utilizes a denoising diffusion model to learn priors for scene geometry and color, normalizing the geometry and color of the scene to achieve better quality in reconstructed geometry under sparse input views [S3]. During NeRF training, random RGBD patches are rendered. Backpropagate the estimated gradients of the log-likelihood to the color and density fields to normalize the geometry and color [S3]. On the LLFF dataset, the PSNR indicators in 3, 6, and 9 input views are 1-2 points higher. Among three input views, the PSNR index is nearly 1 point higher than ViP-NeRF [S3].
 
